<urn:beads-cache:finding:C2-FTQ-007> triage:qa6Review "{\"owner\": \"background C2 rust-developer, with upstream public compatibility restoration owned by sc-runtime\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-6\", \"reviewed_commit\": \"08f7cee0308f52eb0a5a0067cb4e209e2c82806e\", \"reviewer_records\": [{\"finding\": {\"evidence\": \"owned_runtime.rs79 receives application state,80 spawns a single super::request,81-84 expects entered. readiness.rs94-113 creates sync_channel(0), spawns a thread whose first receiver.recv is101, and immediately returns state without a receiver-ready handshake; ReadyState::ready62-69 maps TrySendError::Full to Busy. Application::start_inner79-106 retains this behavior. The authoritative sprint doc288-290 explicitly requires READINESS_BUSY when the worker is not idle/receiving; this is a fixture assumption, not a new requirement to accept every probe. Public DaemonFixture startup/endpoint ownership cannot synchronize the separate std thread. Static causal finding; no current execution or observed frequency is claimed because the unchanged published-SDK compile blocker prevents this test from running.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests/owned_runtime.rs\", \"id\": \"C2-FTQ-007\", \"issue\": \"The new portable scenario issues exactly one initial /ready request and then waits for observed read entry. Application startup only spawns the readiness thread; no receiver-idle synchronization precedes that request. If the HTTP request runs before the dedicated thread reaches recv(), try_send on its zero-capacity channel returns BUSY and the client completes normally. No evaluation runs and the entry sender remains unsent, so the correct service causes the fixture to fail its2s admission timeout. Runtime listener readiness does not establish this independent worker readiness.\", \"line\": 80, \"mechanism\": \"parallel_race\", \"recommendation\": \"Redesign fixture startup/admission synchronization so the test can causally obtain and observe one actual admitted read under the existing finite bound. Preserve the allowed production BUSY response and zero-queued-work contract. If a suitable deterministic admission/idle seam is absent, route the minimal correction to the readiness owner rather than growing compensating test logic. Do not add BUSY retries, busy-poll loops, sleeps or timeout padding.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"status\": \"open_new_fixture_race\", \"test\": \"canceled_read_joins_under_portable_runtime_ownership\"}, \"reviewer\": \"flaky-test-qa\"}], \"scope\": \"Preserve occurrence-specific source corrections and actual platform limits; final sole-enforcer report pending publication.\", \"screen\": \"all_not_applicable; no waiver or suppression\", \"severity\": \"Important\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

